From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:51:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] protocol: serialize device-address commands and maintenance
 features

Append device-address command IDs after the ones upstream assigns, without
changing any existing ID or alias. Transport the maintenance8 capability
structures and their chained inputs through the paired driver and renderer
codecs, and keep VkMemoryBarrierAccessFlags3KHR reachable from VkMemoryBarrier2
even though vk.xml cannot list a context-dependent child in structextends.

Upstream now carries maintenance 8 to 11 and VkCmdEndRendering2, so what
remains here is VK_KHR_device_address_commands, whose twenty-one command IDs
follow upstream's last assignment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
